  "name": "Question 1",
  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14151975/assets/de307da2bc912e9eb6f7312a16be40908d6ccd43cbc613367d042ed55090f2ee.png)\n\nGiven the diagram above, which of the following statements is true?",
  "worked_solution": "Suppose $p$ and $q$ are two lines. Then,\n\n- $p∥q$ means $p$ and $q$ are parallel, and\n\n- $p⊥q$ means $p$ and $q$ are perpendicular.\n\nThe lines $a,c$ and $b,d$ are parallel since they will never intersect. Therefore, the correct statement is $a∥c$ and $b∥d.$",
